---
import { GITHUB_REPO_URL } from '../config/github';

const COS_URL = `${GITHUB_REPO_URL}/tree/main/chief-of-staff`;
---

<section id="chief-of-staff" class="px-6 py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="mb-4 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.3em] text-accent uppercase">Governance by Code</p>
    <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-text sm:text-4xl">
      The gate is an agent,<br />
      <span class="text-accent">not a committee.</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
      <p>
        Every application runs through our Chief of Staff agent. It reads your issue,
        assesses your claims against a written rubric, optionally screens your repo,
        and produces a structured report the council reviews before the demo.
      </p>
      <p>
        <span class="text-text font-semibold">The agent gates the rubric, not the verdict.</span>
        Humans still run the demo. Humans still pick Champions. Humans still vote on membership.
        The agent's job is removing favoritism and keeping the bar stable as the guild grows.
        Same standard for every applicant. No hidden rules. No back channels.
      </p>
      <p>
        The code is open source. The rubric is open source. Read it before you apply.
        If you think the bar is wrong, you can see exactly why we set it there and argue
        the spec on GitHub.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <a
        href={COS_URL}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-block border border-border bg-surface px-6 py-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-text-muted transition-colors hover:border-accent/40 hover:text-accent uppercase"
      >
        Read the Chief of Staff &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
